From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgx-build <build@dgx-01.local>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] qwen3.8-flash-next: route the small-N BF16 linears through
 b12x gemm.bf16_gemv

Two unquantized BF16 projections dominate the non-MoE GEMM bucket at decode:

  hyper-connection down/block-inject  [336, 10240]  97 launches/step  3.79 ms
  MoE router gate                     [512,  2560]  48 launches/step  0.85 ms

Both are unquantized, so they reach cuBLAS, which for M=5 selects
cutlass_80_wmma_tensorop_bf16_s161616gemm_bf16_16x16_128x2_tn_align8 -- a
one-warp-per-CTA SM80 WMMA kernel. Measured on rank0 (98 decode steps, c1):
39.09 us for 6.64 MB of weights and 17.82 us for 2.62 MB, i.e. 170 and 147
GB/s against a 273 GB/s LPDDR5x roofline.

b12x already ships a CuTe small-N GEMV sized for exactly this envelope
(gemm.bf16_gemv: N <= SMALL_N_GEMV_MAX_OUT=1024, K >= SMALL_N_GEMV_MIN_IN=1024,
M <= SMALL_M_MAX=8), and its own comment names "narrow projections like the
GDN in_proj_ba" as the target. The only route to it is
B12XFp6Config.get_quant_method in b12x/integration/vllm/plugin.py, which is
never instantiated for a modelopt MIXED_PRECISION checkpoint. This binds the
same component directly for the two shapes above.

This is NOT bit-identical -- the GEMV accumulates in a different order -- so
it is gated by VLLM_QWEN38_BF16_GEMV (default "hc,gate"; "off", "hc" or
"gate" to bisect) and must clear the full quality gate plus
scripts/logits_equiv.py.

Every guard that cannot be evaluated under Dynamo (16B alignment, whether
this exact M was prepared) lives inside the custom op, whose fallback is
torch.nn.functional.linear -- so any shape the GEMV cannot serve, including
prefill and c8 decode (M=40 > SMALL_M_MAX), is bit-identical to stock.

Applies on top of 8e1f1e587f.
Fix on top of the first cut: b12x's candidate race requires every PreparedCall
to carry an activation producer (b12x/preparation/_measurement.py:226,
"candidate races require an activation-producing context").  The first cut
built its benchmark source once with torch.randn and passed no `produce`, so
with B12X_AUTOTUNE=1 preparation died as soon as it raced the gemm.bf16_gemv
candidates:

  b12x compiling gemm.bf16_gemv: candidates 2/3 prepared, 2 compilations
  b12x failed gemm.bf16_gemv
  RuntimeError: b12x preparation failed on rank 0:
      ValueError: candidate races require an activation-producing context

The benchmark call now follows the in-tree reference wiring in
models/deepseek_v4_1/b12x_layers.py: an empty source refilled by
`produce=lambda: source.normal_(std=0.25)`, and a caller-owned output so the
allocator stays out of the timed region.  Autotune races these units.

